246
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,830
Wait.

247
00:13:20,913 --> 00:13:22,245
I still have this time wizard.

248
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:25,857
Too bad I don't have my baby
dragon to play it with anymore.

249
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:26,770
Oh, well.

250
00:13:26,853 --> 00:13:29,397
I guess it couldn't hurt to
put it out on the field anyway.

251
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,539
Here goes nothing.

252
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,070
Time wizard!

253
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:34,770
Hmm.

254
00:13:34,853 --> 00:13:36,437
That's the card Joey beat me with.

255
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,720
I should warn Rex. Raptor!

256
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:40,340
Watch that time wizard!

257
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:44,217
Ah, without Yugi's help, this chump
doesn't even know how to use it.

258
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:45,760
I know Joey's type.

259
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:47,457
He'll try and play a monster next,

260
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:51,037
and then he'll be in for the
prehistoric pounding of his life.

261
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,620
Maybe Rex is right.

262
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:55,400
Joey was able to defeat my harpy ladies,

263
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:58,177
but only because Yugi
coached him through it.

264
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:00,060
This time, Joey's all alone.

265
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,301
I'm playing rock ogre in defense.

266
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:03,960
You see?

267
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:07,840
I knew the rookie didn't know
what he was doing, Mega-Zalder!

268
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:11,140
Wreck that rock old-school style!

269
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:13,380
Horn-ramming charge, attack!

270
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,260
Reduced to rubble!

271
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:23,674
I sure sent him back to the Stone Ages!

272
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,230
Fine!

273
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,180
Go, flame swordsman!

274
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:31,227
Turn up the heat and carve that
dino like it was a big turkey!

275
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:33,897
Didn't you see what I
did to your rock ogre?

276
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:38,377
Do you really think that your puny little
flame swordsman will last any longer?

277
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:42,257
Looks like I'm gonna have to teach
you respect for my Toons the hard way.

278
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:43,170
Attack!

279
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:51,860
Rex, you big dino dummy!

280
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:53,780
Flaming Sword of Battle!

281
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:06,568
Tell me how a swordsman
can beat a dinosaur!

282
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,800
I actually won that?

283
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:11,357
There is no way Joey could have known that

284
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:14,277
dinosaur cards are especially
vulnerable to fire.

285
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:17,007
That jerk, he totally
lucked out on that one.

286
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:20,157
Looks like I found the
secret to beating your Toons.

287
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,977
Hope you're not too sore about it.

288
00:15:22,060 --> 00:15:24,540
Get it? Sword? Dino? Dinosaur?

289
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:27,020
Sword arm of dragon! Want some?

290
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,513
Come and get it, buddy.

291
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:34,810
Yeah!

292
00:15:34,893 --> 00:15:37,057
I knew you were gonna
make a comeback, Joey!

293
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:39,240
This is far from over, you know.

294
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:41,257
One card won't win this for you.

295
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:44,237
Alrighty then, I'll just
bring out another for you.

296
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,600
Swamp Battle God!

297
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:50,040
Big deal!

298
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:54,084
I have a beast that'll wipe that
smirk off your face permanently!

299
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:57,850
Alright!

300
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,118
Meet the top link of the food chain!

301
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,640
Serpent Night Dragon!

302
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:09,357
This rare card's awarded to
the elite few who have made

303
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,977
it to the final round of
the regional championships.

304
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:16,472
But for a loser like you, it should be
an honor just to get thrashed by it.

305
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:18,840
Nightmare Sonic Blast!

306
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:26,920
He was my best card.

307
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:28,620
Oh, poor Joey.

308
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:33,108
Man, there's not a monster in
my deck that could save me now.

309
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:36,950
Huh?

310
00:16:37,033 --> 00:16:37,863
Tristan's card.

311
00:16:37,946 --> 00:16:39,700
Man, he always shows up somehow.

312
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:44,480
Hey, there's no concern, you hair job.

313
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:47,737
Yeah, didn't no one ever teach you not
to mess with other people's business?

314
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:49,677
Didn't anyone teach you
that you shouldn't be

315
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:52,597
picking on defenseless
little kids half your size?

316
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:54,915
Then how about we pick on you instead?

317
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:57,480
Hey, everything all right, Joey?

318
00:16:58,340 --> 00:16:59,170
Yeah?

319
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,539
Mess them both up!

320
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:01,960
Watch that guy!

321
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:03,470
Let's go!

322
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:13,500
You okay, Joey?

323
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,757
You should have called me.

324
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:16,722
I'd have been here earlier, man.

325
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:19,597
What are you doing here, Tristan?

326
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,268
What are you talking about?

327
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:23,425
I could have taken those guys.

328
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:27,638
I appreciate you trying to help me
out, but I don't need to be babied.

329
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:36,057
man all this time it finally hits me
tristan's always been looking out for

330
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:40,728
me not because he thinks i always need
his help but because he's a true friend

331
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:47,417
yo joey huh what we're here
for you buddy so how about it

332
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:50,357
you're gonna take that car to mine
Wait for a test drive or what?

333
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,270
Hey!

334
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:53,820
You got it, pal.

335
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:56,780
Go Lava Battle God!

336
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,240
Cool, my card's on the field.

337
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:02,920
What a touching reunion.

338
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:06,769
Too bad my serpent night dragon
is gonna blast it to shreds.

339
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:09,100
Now, attack the green one.

340
00:18:14,940 --> 00:18:15,770
What?

341
00:18:15,853 --> 00:18:17,838
My sonic blasts are being deflected.

342
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:24,260
How was my dragon's attack repelled?

343
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,077
There aren't any trap cards out.

344
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:26,990
Oh, yeah!

345
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:29,437
Oh, I get it.

346
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,737
The red one blocked for the green one.

347
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:34,577
Tristan's card was there
right when I needed it most.

348
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:35,490
Of course.

349
00:18:35,573 --> 00:18:37,237
Those two monsters are like best friends,

350
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:40,137
so when they're together on the
field, they help power each other up.

351
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:44,573
Just like how you and Joey help each
other out in real life, huh, Tristan?

352
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:47,134
That's what being a buddy is all about.

353
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:49,337
Thanks for everything, man.

354
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:50,250
I owe you.

355
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:53,520
What a team!

356
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,737
Not only did you take out Rex's monster,

357
00:18:55,820 --> 00:18:57,977
but you made a nice
debt in his life points,

358
00:18:58,060 --> 00:18:58,890
too.

359
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:00,190
Right.

360
00:19:00,273 --> 00:19:04,944
And now that we're together again, there's
not a monster Rex has that can stop us.

361
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:10,900
Celebrate while you can, because
your party's about to be crashed!
